Feature: Check Credit # features/check_credit.feature:1

  Scenario: Order placed within the credit limit                # features/check_credit.feature:3
    Given a new customer with credit limit 1000                 # features/steps/check_credit.py:7
    When an order is placed with 2 Widget                       # features/steps/check_credit.py:44
    Then the item amount is 180                                 # features/steps/check_credit.py:94
    And the order total is 180                                  # features/steps/check_credit.py:106
    And the customer balance is 180                             # features/steps/check_credit.py:112
    And Logic adjusts the customer balance from the order total # features/steps/check_credit.py:142

  Scenario: Item quantity change flows to the order total and balance  # features/check_credit.feature:11
    Given a new customer with credit limit 1000                        # features/steps/check_credit.py:7
    And an order is placed with 2 Widget                               # features/steps/check_credit.py:44
    When the item quantity is changed to 5                             # features/steps/check_credit.py:54
    Then the item amount is 450                                        # features/steps/check_credit.py:94
    And the order total is 450                                         # features/steps/check_credit.py:106
    And the customer balance is 450                                    # features/steps/check_credit.py:112

  Scenario: Shipping an order removes it from the balance  # features/check_credit.feature:19
    Given a new customer with credit limit 1000            # features/steps/check_credit.py:7
    And an order is placed with 2 Widget                   # features/steps/check_credit.py:44
    When the order is shipped                              # features/steps/check_credit.py:60
    Then the customer balance is 0                         # features/steps/check_credit.py:112

  Scenario: Moving an order to another customer moves the balance  # features/check_credit.feature:25
    Given a new customer with credit limit 1000                    # features/steps/check_credit.py:7
    And a second customer with credit limit 1000                   # features/steps/check_credit.py:15
    And an order is placed with 2 Widget                           # features/steps/check_credit.py:44
    When the order is moved to the second customer                 # features/steps/check_credit.py:66
    Then the customer balance is 0                                 # features/steps/check_credit.py:112
    And the second customer balance is 180                         # features/steps/check_credit.py:118

  Scenario: Order over the credit limit is rejected          # features/check_credit.feature:33
    Given a new customer with credit limit 100               # features/steps/check_credit.py:7
    When an order is placed with 2 Widget                    # features/steps/check_credit.py:44
    Then the request is rejected with "exceeds credit limit" # features/steps/check_credit.py:124
    And the customer balance is 0                            # features/steps/check_credit.py:112

  Scenario: Balance equal to the credit limit is accepted  # features/check_credit.feature:39
    Given a new customer with credit limit 180             # features/steps/check_credit.py:7
    When an order is placed with 2 Widget                  # features/steps/check_credit.py:44
    Then the request is accepted                           # features/steps/check_credit.py:131
    And the customer balance is 180                        # features/steps/check_credit.py:112

  Scenario: Lowering the credit limit below the balance is rejected  # features/check_credit.feature:45
    Given a new customer with credit limit 1000                      # features/steps/check_credit.py:7
    And an order is placed with 2 Widget                             # features/steps/check_credit.py:44
    When the credit limit is changed to 100                          # features/steps/check_credit.py:72
    Then the request is rejected with "exceeds credit limit"         # features/steps/check_credit.py:124

  Scenario: Product price change does not alter existing items  # features/check_credit.feature:51
    Given a new customer with credit limit 1000                 # features/steps/check_credit.py:7
    And a new product priced 50                                 # features/steps/check_credit.py:20
    And an order is placed with 2 of the new product            # features/steps/check_credit.py:49
    When the product price is changed to 80                     # features/steps/check_credit.py:77
    Then the item unit price is 50                              # features/steps/check_credit.py:100
    And the item amount is 100                                  # features/steps/check_credit.py:94

  Scenario: Deleting an order deletes its items  # features/check_credit.feature:59
    Given a new customer with credit limit 1000  # features/steps/check_credit.py:7
    And an order is placed with 2 Widget         # features/steps/check_credit.py:44
    When the order is deleted                    # features/steps/check_credit.py:83
    Then the order has no items                  # features/steps/check_credit.py:136
    And the customer balance is 0                # features/steps/check_credit.py:112

  Scenario: Item for an unknown product is rejected    # features/check_credit.feature:66
    Given a new customer with credit limit 1000        # features/steps/check_credit.py:7
    And an empty order                                 # features/steps/check_credit.py:27
    When an item is added for product id 999999        # features/steps/check_credit.py:89
    Then the request is rejected with "Missing Parent" # features/steps/check_credit.py:124

Feature: Order B2B Intake # features/order_b2b_intake.feature:1

  Scenario: Partner order through the REST API is created                      # features/order_b2b_intake.feature:3
    Given a new customer with credit limit 1000                                # features/steps/check_credit.py:7
    When a partner order for the customer with 1 Widget and 2 Gadget is posted # features/steps/order_b2b_intake.py:24
    Then the partner request answers 201                                       # features/steps/order_b2b_intake.py:55
    And the partner order total is 390                                         # features/steps/order_b2b_intake.py:61
    And the customer balance is 390                                            # features/steps/check_credit.py:112

  Scenario: Partner order for an unknown account is refused                    # features/order_b2b_intake.feature:10
